1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Hund Şehzade''' was an Ottoman princess, granddaughter of claimant to the throne [https://www.geni.com/people/S%C3%BCleyman-%C3%87elebi-co-sultan-of-Rumelia/4872592682460047336 Süleyman Çelebi], and great-grandd
2 CONC aughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Bayezid-1-ottoman-sultan/385217766960003428 Sultan Bayezid I] (r.1389 – 1402) of the Ottoman Empire. She was wife of [https://www.geni.com/people/Al-Ashraf-Sayf-ad-D%C4%ABn-Barsb%C4%81y/6000
2 CONC 000204999033899 Barsbay], and later of [https://www.geni.com/people/Sayf-ad-Din-Jaqmaq-Mamluk-Sultan-of-Egypt-and-Syria/6000000204996980823 Sayf ad-Din Jaqmaq], Egypt Sultans of the Burji dynasty.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hund_%C5%9Eehzade En]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hund_%C5%9Eehzade#Early_life Early life]===
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in 1422 as '''Fatima Şehzade''', she was the daughter of Orhan Çelebi, son of Süleyman Çelebi,[4] who was himself the son of Sultan Bayezid I. She had a younger brother named [https://www.geni.com/people/S%C3%BCleyman-%C3%87e
2 CONC lebi/6000000204999738829 Süleyman Çelebi] (1423 – 1437).[5][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1433,[7] Şehzade and her brother Süleyman took refuge in Cairo.[8][9] The Mamluk Sultan Barsbay treated them generously, and rejected her cousin Murad II's requests to surrender them.[7] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hund_%C5%9Eehzade#First_marriage First marriage]===
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1436, Ibrahim II of Karaman, attacked the Dulkadirids, and captured the disputable town of Kayseri and other fortresses in its vicinity. However, the Dulkadirids retook Kayseri and the surrounding countryside from the Karamanid
2 CONC s in December 1436 with Ottoman help. Upon receiving this news Barsbay in March 1437, assembled his advisory council, and decided to send the governors of Syria to help Ibrahim Bey. However, before the crisis escalated, and turned
2 CONC  into a military clash, both Ottoman and Mamluk Sultans settled their differences two months later in May. A peace agreement was settled, with Barsbay's marriage to Şehzade.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hund_%C5%9Eehzade#Second_marriage Second marriage]===
2 CONT
2 CONT After Barbay's death in 1438,[10] his successor Sultan Sayf-al-Din Jaqmaq married Şehzade, in order to consolidate good relations with the Ottomans.[11] On 5 January 1447, she made a pilgrimage with the dowry she received at the t
2 CONC ime of her marriage to Jaqmaq.[12] 
2 CONT
2 CONT The two together had four sons. All of them died of plague at Cairo on 26 March 1449. The eldest one named Ahmed being seven years old. Jaqmaq divorced her on 25 December 1450.[13] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hund_%C5%9Eehzade#Third_marriage Third marriage]===
2 CONT
2 CONT After Jaqmaq divorced Şehzade, she settled in a house in al-Jawdariyya, and married Sahib-al-Hujjab Barsbay Bujashi.[13] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hund_%C5%9Eehzade#Death Death]===
2 CONT
2 CONT Şehzade died in July 1455 in Cairo.[14] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hund_%C5%9Eehzade#References References]===
2 CONT
