1 NOTE {geni:about_me}   Bayezid I had at least five daughters:[37]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fatma Hündi Hatun''' (1375–1430). She married to Seyyid Şemseddin Mehmed Buhari Emir Sultan in 1390 and she had four sons, Emir Ali and other three, and two daughters. Legend has it that Hundi and Seyyid were married in secret 
2 CONC after having a vision of the Islamic prophet Muhammad, and that Bayezid only accepted their marriage after a miracle saved his son-in-law from soldiers sent to kill him. According to another version, Seyyd, guest of Bayezid, took 
2 CONC advantage of his absence from court to seduce Hundi and marry her.
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayezid_I#Daughters
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatma_Hundi_Hatun
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:''' She was not married to [https://www.geni.com/people/Stjepan-Hercegovi%C4%87/6000000010115264547 Stjepan Ahmed Hercegović].
