1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hatice Sultan (1496–1538) (Ottoman Turkish: خدیجہ سلطان) was an Ottoman princess, daughter of Sultan Selim I and Ayşe Hafsa Sultan. She was the sister of Sultan Suleiman the Magnificent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hatice Sultan was born in 1496. First, she married Iskender Beğ but became widow by his death. Then, she married Pargalı Ibrahim Pasha, who was the Grand Vizier from 1523 and remained in office for 13 years, but in 1536 he was exe
2 CONC cuted by the Sultan and his property was confiscated by the state. The couple had two children. They lived in their palace in Istanbul. There are speculations that Hatice committed suicide because she was in sorrow for her beloved
2 CONC  husband. She died in 1538
