1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fülane Hatun (Ottoman Turkish: فولاني خاتون) (born 1496 - died 1550) was the first wife of Suleiman the Magnificent, the Sultan of the Ottoman Empire. She was the mother of Şehzade Mahmud, who died young of smallpo
2 CONC x, and Fatma Sultan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her real name is unknown; fülane was used as a compliment for women. She was born in 1496, and was Greek from Smyrna, belonging to the so-called Rum Millet.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was Suleiman's first concubine, and entered the harem in or around 1510. Suleiman was still a Şehzade or ("Ottoman prince") and the governor of Manisa sanjak (then known as Saruhan) when she gave birth to her son Şehzade Mahmu
2 CONC d in 1512 and her daughter Fatma in 1516. Mahmud died of smallpox in 1521 at the age of nine, and Fatma Sultan died in 1561 .
2 CONT
2 CONT She was sent to the old palace. She died in 1550 in Edirne.
