1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Soltana sives Sultana family originated in Malta from the captured slave Solimano bin Musa from Turkey (b.1507; d.1559). Solimano, a younger son of an Amir or Bey in Karaman-Turkey, served as a slave to several
2 CONC  Grandmasters while in Rhodes and eventually accompanied the Order to Malta. In 1539, Grandmaster de Homedes freed him with a condition that he had to serve another six years. Upon release, the Grandmaster had granted him some lan
2 CONC ds in Xaghra, Gozo for services rendered. Solimano married in 1540 to Mustafa, an ex-slave from Turkey. Both were baptised Christians.
