2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SERBIA.htm#DjuradjVukovicdied1456
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         GRGUR ([1415]-Čilandar 16/17 Oct 1459).  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names (in order) Gregory, Stephen, Lazar, Maria, and Cantacuzina as the children of George of Serbia & his wife, stating that Gregory died unmarr
2 CONC ied[433].  The manuscript Vaticanus latinus 4789 records names (in order) “Etienne...Grégoire...Lazare” as the three sons of “le seigneur Georges Cantacuzène...[sa sœur] Irène” and her husband “[le] despote de Serbie”, adding that
2 CONC  “leur gendre...le grand turc” captured “Etienne et...Grégoire” and blinded them[434].  Theodoros Spandounes names "il primo…il Despoto Stefano, el secundo…il Despoto Curgur…il terzo…Lazaro Despoto" as the three sons of "Despoto J
2 CONC urgo" and his wife, adding that Grgur was blinded by the Ottomans and died in Hungary without legitimate children[435].  “Georgius, Serbiæ despotes” donated to “monasterio montis Atho Esphigmeni” by charter dated 11 Sep 1429, with
2 CONC  “imagines Georgii et conjugis Irenæ et filiorum Gregorii, Stephani (et Lazari) et “filiarum Maræ et Cantacuzenæ”[436].  He was installed by the Ottomans as Governor in the former Branković lands in southern Serbia in 1439.  Accus
2 CONC ed of plotting against the sultan, his governorship was confiscated in Apr 1441, he was taken to Amaseia in Asia Minor and blinded 8 May 1441[437].  “Georgius, Serbiæ despotæ, et filii Gregorius, Stephanus et Lazarus” confirmed th
2 CONC e privileges of the Ragusans by charter dated 17 Sep 1445[438].  He became a monk as GERMAN at Čilandar[439].  He and his son may have tried to seize power in Serbia after the death of his brother Lazar, maybe with Turkish support
2 CONC [440].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' JELISAVETA, daughter of ---.  According to the Masarelli Vatican manuscript, Grgur was unmarried and it mentions no children[441].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Grgur had one possible illegitimate child by an unknown mistress:
