1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fatma Haseki Sultan or Fatma Sultan (Ottoman Turkish: فاطمة خاصكي سلطان, born 1530 Mari, Syria - died Istanbul, the Ottoman Empire) was the wife of Şehzade Bayezid and the mother of Şehzade Orhan, Şehzade Osman, Şe
2 CONC hzade Abdullah, Mihrumah Sultan and Ayşe Sultan
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Sultan Suleiman and Hürrem Sultan's son Şehzade Bayezid. Her life after the death of Şehzade Bayezid is unknown. She died in 1585 in Istanbul. Her death place is the tomb of Melik-i Acem, Sivas.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fatma Hatun''' (Ottoman Turkish: فاطمة خاتون‎, born 1530 Caucasus - died Istanbul, the Ottoman Empire) was the wife of Şehzade Bayezid and the mother of Şehzade Orhan, Şehzade Osman, Şehzade Abdullah, Mihrumah Sultan and Ayşe S
2 CONC ultan. She was of Circassian origin and was probably related to Mahidevran Sultan, the stepmother of her spouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Sultan Suleiman and Hürrem Sultan's son Şehzade Bayezid. Her life after the death of Şehzade Bayezid is unknown. She died in 1585 in Istanbul. Her burial place is the tomb of Melik-i Acem, Sivas along with her h
2 CONC usband's tomb.
2 CONT
