1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Uros
2 CONT
2 CONT John Uroš married a daughter of Radoslav Hlapen, a Serbian lord in Macedonia. According to the manuscript Dell'Imperadori Constantinopolitani, preserved in the papers of Angelo Masarelli, the father of John's wife was "lord of Dri
2 CONC ma" ("l Signor Drimi"). 
2 CONT
2 CONT John had five children:[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Constantine (Konstantin)
2 CONT # Michael (Mihajlo)
2 CONT # Demetrios (Dimitrije)
2 CONT # Helena (Jelena) Ouresina Palaiologina, who married Theodore Kantakouzenos, with whom she had Irene Kantakouzene
2 CONT # Asanina
2 CONT # 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radoslav_Hlapen He married Irina (Irene), the widow of caesar Preljub. They had the following issue:  ... Unnamed, married John Uroš[1]
2 CONT *1.  Evans, Charles F. H. (1989). Studies in Genealogy and Family History in Tribute to Charles Evans on the Occasion of His Eightieth Birthday. Association for the Promotion of Scholarship in Genealogy. [https://books.google.com/
2 CONC books?id=pK1pAAAAMAAJ GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Uroš
2 CONT *4.  the Masarelli manuscript, 'Dell'Imperadori Constantinopolitani', from papers of 'Massarellus', Angelo Massarelli (1510-1566), held now in the Vatican Library, reports: "Cesare Urione de Phersali hebbe dui figlioli, Demetrio e
2 CONC t Giovani, il quale prese per moglia da figlia del S'or Drimi, hebbe cinque figlioli, cioe Helena, Constantino, Michel, Asanina, Demetrio. Helena fu maritata in Theodoro Catacusino."
