1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Milica_of_Serbia
2 CONT Princess '''Milica Hrebeljanović''' née '''Nemanjić''' (Serbian: Милица Немањић Хребељановић · ca. 1335 – November 11, 1405) also known as '''Empress (Tsaritsa) Milica''', was a royal consort of Serbia by marriage to Prince Lazar 
2 CONC who fell in the Battle of Kosovo. After her husband's death, she took the role as queen regent of Serbia from 1389 to 1393, until her son, despot Stefan Lazarević came of age.
2 CONT
2 CONT She later became a Serbian Orthodox nun under the name Jevgenija. She is the author of "A Mother's Prayer" (Serbian: Молитва матере) and a famous poem of mourning for her husband, My Widowhood's Bridegroom (Serbian: Удовству мојем
2 CONC у женик).
2 CONT
