1 NOTE Milica, wife of Prince Lazar Hrebaljanovic of Serbia, was a great-granddaughter of Dmitri Nemanjic, himself son of Vukan II Nemanjic.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vukan II Nemanjic was king of the Zeta (1196-1208) and Grand Župan of Serbia (1202-1204).
2 CONT He had three sons: Ðorde, Stefan, and Dmitri. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Kostadin, father of Vasoje, the founder of the Vasojevic family, was probably the son of Vukan, according to some historian, but was more probably his grandson from his (Vukan's) son, Stefan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vukan II Nemanjic was the son of Serbian Grand Župan "Stefan Nemanja"
2 CONT Stefan Nemanja (1113\1117-13 February 1199\1200) was a Medieval Serb nobleman, descended from the Vukanovic who was Grand Prince  of the medieval Serb state of Rascia in 1168-1196. He established control over the territories of ne
2 CONC ighboring Serb states, including Zeta/Doclea, and unified them into a single state. He founded the Nemanjic dynasty and became an Orthodox Saint (Symeon) after numerous miracles following his death.
