2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Lala Mustafa Pasha (c. 1500 – 7 August 1580), also known by the additional epithet Kara, was an Ottoman general and Grand Vizier from the Sanjak of Bosnia.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wiki [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lala_Mustafa_Pasha page]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lala_Mustafa_Pasha#Life Life]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lala_Mustafa_Pasha#Death Death]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lala_Mustafa_Pasha#Issue Issue]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lala Mustafa Pasha was the second husband of Hümaşah Sultan, Ottoman princess, daughter of Şehzade Mehmed and granddaughter of Sultan Süleyman I and Hürrem Sultan. They married on 25 August 1575. By her, he had a son:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sultanzade Abdülbaki Bey. He married Safiye Hanımsultan, daughter of his mother's cousin Ismihan Sultan (daughter of Sultan Selim II and Nurbanu Sultan)
2 CONT
