1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanijeli_Siyavu%C5%9F_Pasha '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kanijeli Siyavuş Pasha''' (Bosnian: ''Sijavuš-paša Kanjižanin'', died 1602, Istanbul) was an Ottoman statesman from the Sanjak of Bosnia. He was Grand Vizier between 24 December 1582 and 28 July 1584,[1] 15 April 1586 and 2 Apr
2 CONC il 1589,[2] and 4 April 1592 and 28 January 1593.[2] He was from Kanjiža in modern-day Hungary, then part of first the Sanjak and then the Eyalet of Bosnia.[3] He was married to Fatma Sultan, daughter of Selim II.
2 CONT
2 CONT =See also=
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Ottoman_Grand_Viziers '''List of Ottoman Grand Viziers''']
2 CONT
