1 OCCU grand vizier 1598-1599 of the Ottoman Empire 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerrah_Mehmed_Pasha En]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Cerrah Mehmed Pasha''' (Ottoman Turkish: جراح محمد پاشا; died January 1604, Istanbul) was an Ottoman statesman. He was grand vizier of the Ottoman Empire from 1598 to 1599.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mehmed Pasha was the palace surgeon prior to becoming grand vizier, hence his epithet cerrah 'surgeon'. The Istanbul neighborhood of Cerrahpaşa and one of the two medical faculties of Istanbul University, Cerrahpaşa Medical Facult
2 CONC y [tr] (the other being Istanbul Medical Faculty [tr]), are named after him.
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1579 he married Gevherhan Sultan, a daughter of Sultan Selim II and Nurbanu Sultan. He was her second husband.[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had at least a son:[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sultanzade Salih Bey. Governor of Klis.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerrah_Mehmed_Pasha#References References]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * from the Wikipedia page of his wife, Gevherhan Sultan:
2 CONT
2 CONT Piyale Pasha died in 1578 and Gevherhan Sultan is said to have married Boyalı Mehmed Pasha in 1579.
