2 CONT Nikita Romanovich 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nikita Romanovich also known as Nikita Romanovich Zakharyin-Yuriev (Russian: Никита Романович, died 23 April 1586) was a Muscovite Boyar in 1563 whose grandson Mikhail Feodorovich founded the Romanov dynasty of Russian tsars. He w
2 CONC as son of the Boyar Roman Yurievich Zakharyin-Yuriev, Okolnichi, who died on 16 February 1543, who gave his name to the Romanov Dynasty of Russian monarchs, and wife Uliana Ivanovna, who died in 1579, and the brother-in-law of Iva
2 CONC n IV of Russia, who had married his sister Anastasia Romanovna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anastasia of Russia 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anastasia Romanovna Zakharyina-Yurieva (died 7 August 1560) was the first wife of the Russian Tsar Ivan the Terrible and the first Russian tsarina. She was the daughter of Boyar Roman Yurievich Zakharyin-Yuriev, Okolnichi, who die
2 CONC d on 16 February 1543, who gave his name to the Romanov Dynasty of Russian monarchs, and wife Uliana Ivanovna, who died in 1579.
2 CONT
2 CONT E4. Roman Yurievich Zakharin, okolnichi, +16.2.1543; m.Uliana Ivanovna (+1579) 
