1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Vasily Glinsky was known from 1480. Courtier of the Grand Duke of Lithuania Casimir, later of the Grand Duke of Lithuania Alexander, in 1501–1507. Joiner of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania, in 1506–1507. Elder of Bras
2 CONC ta. In 1504. bought by Dubičius. One of the leaders of the rebellion of his brother Michael in 1508. After the uprising was suppressed, he fled with his brother to Moscow. He had three sons and three daughters. One of them, Elena 
2 CONC Glinskaya (d. 1538), married the Grand Duke of Moscow, Vasily III, in 1526.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lev's third son, Ivan Glinsky, served in the court of Casimir of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania from 1482. In 1501–1507. Grand Marshal of Lithuania, in 1505–1507. Voivode of Kiev, Voivode of Novgorod in 1507–1508. As a participant i
2 CONC n the rebellion in 1508, he fled to Moscow with his brothers.
