1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Akhmat Khan , completely Achmed Chan bin Kütschük (also Ahmed Khan ; † January 6, 1481 at the mouth of the Donets ), was from 1465 to 1481 Khan of the Golden Horde .
2 CONT
2 CONT Akhmat Khan wrested the rule from his brother Mahmud Khan , which he had held since 1459. In 1472 Akhmat Khan entered into an alliance with the Polish ruler Casimir IV against the Russian ruler Ivan III. a. However, the alliance c
2 CONC ould not defeat Russia. In 1480 Akhmat Khan organized another campaign against Moscow, which eventually led to the end of the Mongol invasion of Russia after standing almost without a fight on the Ugra . The Mongol threat to Russi
2 CONC a was thus over once and for all. On January 6, 1481, Akhmat Khan and his people were killed by Ibaq Khan , the ruler of the Sibir Khanate , at the mouth of the Donets . His successor Saih Ahmed was executed as the last ruler of t
2 CONC he Golden Horde in Lithuania.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.zxc.wiki/wiki/Akhmat_Khan
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmed_Khan_bin_K%C3%BCch%C3%BCk
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Father of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Murtadâ Khan of the Golden Horde - r. 1481-1499; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sayyid Âhmad III Khan of the Golden Horde - r. 1481-?  [Shayik-Ahmad Last Khan of the Golden Horde - r. 1481-1502]
2 CONT ====
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1465-1481 : Ahmed fils de Kutjukh Mohammed
2 CONT voir:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.histoiredumonde.net/Horde-d-Or.html
2 CONT === 
2 CONT Also Genealogy:
2 CONT
2 CONT Genghis Khan
2 CONT
2 CONT Jochi
2 CONT
2 CONT Orda Khan
