2 CONT [Jahan Shah, the Qara-Quyunlu ruler of AdharbayjSn, set out from Tabriz °, on ShawwSl 8, 872 7 /May 4, 1468, to annex Diyfir Bakr. His vanguard was surprised by Amir Hasan Beg in the desert of Mush 8 , He himself was put to death 
2 CONC while he was staying behind 9 , and his head was sent to Sultan Abu Sa'Id ij, the Timurid ruler of  Khurasan. His two sons, named Muhammad! and Yiisuf. were also* captured, of whom the former was put to death and the latter blinde
2 CONC d 11]ref: https://archive.org/stream/HistoryOfShahIsmailSafawi-GhulamSarwar/119900259-History-of-Shah-Isma-il-Safawi-Ghulam-Sarwar_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT With his death, the great era of Kara Koyunlu history came to an end. [ The Alban dynasty Hasan Jalal https://www.geni.com/people/Hassan-Djalal-Vahtangian-King-of-Syunik-r-1214-1261/6000000100802219980 took over the Melik title fr
2 CONC om the Qara Qoyunlu Jahan Shah ... Jelal Dynasty then separated into five Alban feudal principalities - melikli such as Gulustan, Chileberd, Khachin, Varand and Dizakh. ref page 156 of A Brief History of Karabakh and the Armenian-
2 CONC Azarbaijani Relations by Asim Jannatoglu Jannatov. An Academia.edu article.].
2 CONT =====
2 CONT The Kara Koyunlu or Qara Qoyunlu, also called the Black Sheep Turkomans (Turkmen: Garagoýunly türkmenler, Persian: Qara Qoyunlu, قرا قویونلو), were a Shia[2] Oghuz Turkic tribal federation that ruled over the territory comprising 
2 CONC the present-day Azerbaijan, Armenia (1406), north-western Iran, eastern Turkey and Iraq from about 1375 to 1468.
2 CONT
2 CONT (see documents)
2 CONT
2 CONT [...In 1441, the Turkoman Jahan Shah established the melikdoms of Syunik and Artsakh and placed
2 CONT them under the rule of the meliks officially, allowing them to govern their domains as they saw fit. These territories acted as mini buffer states on the frontiers of his realm. This system survived the collapse of the Black Sheep
2 CONC  dynasty under the rule of their successors, the Ak Koyunlu (White Sheep Turkomans). In 1501 the Safavid dynasty conquered the territories of the White Sheep Turkomans following a decisive battle in Nakhijevan. The region remained
2 CONC  a frontier zone and suffered greatly during the wars between the Ottomans and the Safavids. The Safavids incorporated the melikdoms into several larger fiefdoms designated as khanates whose rulers were Muslims. There were Armenia
2 CONC n melik residents in all of the khanates of the Safavid Persian Empire but only those in Syunik and Artsakh retained autonomy while under Persian suzerainty...] ref: "The Meliks of Eastern Armenia" by Aspet Emin. 2018
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT Also read : https://www.academia.edu/3604069/Armenia_from_the_fall_of_the_Cilician_Kingdom_1375_to_the_forced_emigration_under_Shah_Abbas_1604_1997?email_work_card=thumbnail
2 CONT
