2 CONT The Spandounes family had not played any significant role in the history of the Byzantine Empire before this date, but more is known about Theodore’s mother, '''Eudotia Kantakouzene''', and her side of the family. '''Her grandfath
2 CONC er was George Palaiologos Kantakouzenos''', a great soldier and scholar, as well as a direct descendant of Emperor John VI Kantakouzenos (1347–1354).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/TheodoreSpandounesOnTheOriginsOfTheOttomanEmperors/Theodore+Spandounes+On+the+Origins+of+the+Ottoman+Emperors_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT This passage too is introduced out of chronological context and mainly to illustrate another piece of the Spandounes family history. The Turkish conquest of Bosnia began in 1463, The Duke (‘Herzog’) of St Saba at the time was Stje
2 CONC pan Vukcic (1435-00). His eldest son was '''Ladislas'''; and it was he who '''married Anna Cantacuzene'''  who, according to '''[Theodore] Spandounes, was-a sister of his grandfather (Theodore Cantacuzene)''' and a daughter of Geo
2 CONC rge Palaiologos Cantacuzene.
