2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1522, he refused to convert to Islam as Shah Ismail had demanded. A new Persian invasion ensued, led this time personally by the shah. David and his son, Luarsab I, offered him a fierce resistance at the Battle of Teleti, but w
2 CONC ere finally outnumbered and defeated. The Kartlian capital Tbilisi was taken by treachery and garrisoned by a large Persian force, making east Georgia nominally fall for the first time under Safavid rule. On the death of Ismail in
2 CONC  1524, David liberated Tbilisi and expelled the Persians from the country.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1525, he reconquered Aghjakala, Lower Kartli, and massacred all the Turkoman Qizilbash who had settled there. The same year, he abdicated the throne in favor of his younger brother, George IX, and retired to a monastery under t
2 CONC he name of Damiane. David X died in 1526 and was buried at the Svetitskhoveli Cathedral at Mtskheta.
