1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ögedei Khan (Mongolian: Өгэдэй, Ögedei; also Ogotai or Oktay; Ogodei) (c. 1186 – December 11, 1241) was the third son of Genghis Khan and his first wife Borta-Fudjin, daughter of Day-Noyon. He was second Great Khan
2 CONC  (Khagan) of the Mongol Empire by succeeding his father...
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ogedei_Khan
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT He was named with a different name at birth, but once he grew up he did not like his name and he was re-named as Ögedei, which means "ascension". Ögedei had four (4) main wives and sixty (60) concubines. Ögedei had seven (7) sons.
2 CONC  His wives in order of marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Burakchin - eldest wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Turakina (Turakin) - from Merkit tribe. She we previously married to Dayr-Usun - leader of Merkit tribe, and after he was killed, she was brought for Ögedei Khan. And before this Dayr-Usun gave his daughter Kulan-Hatun to be wi
2 CONC fe of Genghis Khan. Turakin was very bossy, not beautiful, she resisted Ögedei and he had to take her by force. Genghis Khan approved this marriage, although brother Chagatay did not like this. Turakina cause chaos in Genghis Khan
2 CONC , she disobeyed her own family and Genghis family. Turakina was mother of Ögedei's five (5) sons. The remaining two (2) sons were born from concubines.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Muka (Mukha).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Djachin (Jachin)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The third son. Supreme Khan in 1229 bequest of Chinggis. Got in its management of Mongolia and northern China. In 1231 invasion of Northern China to continue winning, three years later the remnants of the Jurchen state ceased to e
2 CONC xist. Wife merkitka Turakina (Turakana), the rules after his death, from 1241 to 1246. According to others, died on December 11?
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ugtai or Ogedei Ögedei Khan, born Ögedei, was the third son of Genghis Khan and second Great Khan of the Mongol Empire, succeeding his father. Wikipedia Born: November 7, 1186, Mongolia Died: December 11, 1241, Mongolia Spouse: Tö
2 CONC regene Khatun (m. 1204) Parents: Genghis Khan, Börte Children: Güyük Khan, Godan Khan, Kadan Khan, Khorachar Khan, Khashi Khan, Melig Khan, Khochu Khan Siblings: Chagatai Khan
