1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tolui, also rendered Toluy, Tului or Tolui Khan (Mongolian: Толуй хаан (1192–1232) was the youngest son of Genghis Khan by Börte... His name means "Mirror"
2 CONT ===
2 CONT TOLUI, son of JENGHIZ Khan & his first wife Börke Fujin ([1190]-[Sep/Oct] 1232).  Abul-Ghazi Bahadur names “Touli” as the fourth son of “Tchinguiz Khan”[288].  He captured Merv and Nishapur, with his brother-in-law Toghutshar, dur
2 CONC ing the campaign in the Hindu Kush.  His personal patrimony after the death of his father in 1227 was the Mongol heartland around the Onon river.
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONGOLS.htm#Hulagudied1265A
2 CONT ====
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tolui
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Tolui had many concubines and wives. But the chief one was Sorghaghtani who was the mother of Tolui's four ruling sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tolui's sons included:
2 CONT
2 CONT Möngke, the Great Khan of the Mongol Empire.
2 CONT Jurikha
2 CONT Qutughtu Kublai, the Great Khan of the Mongols and the Emperor of the Yuan Dynasty. Hulagu, the first Ilkhan of Mongol Persia. Ariq Böke, Khagan claimant who was supported by the traditionalist Mongols against Kublai. Bujek. He di
2 CONC ed earlier. Nothing is known much about him except his role in Mongol invasion of Europe in 1236–41 and Möngke's election in 1250. Mukha Satukhtai Sabukhtai
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The only brunette among Bordjigin. Was born, when Genghis was a prisoner, but he admitted his son, was the favorite son. In a campaign in 1225 to Chinggis. In 1231 the head of the troops, along with Ugedei invaded northern China, 
2 CONC an unsuccessful siege of Mr. Bian (present-day Kaifeng), later-capture it. Wife, the daughter of Khan Togrul
