2 CONT Names: Suleyman Shah bin Kaya Alp
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Suleyman Shah''' (Ottoman Turkish: سلیمان شاه; Modern Turkish: Süleyman Şah) was, according to Ottoman tradition, the son of Kaya Alp and the father of Ertuğrul, who was the father of Osman I, the founder of the Ottoman Empire
2 CONC .[1] Early Ottoman genealogies disputed this lineage, and either Suleyman Shah or Gündüz Alp could be Osman's grandfather and the father of Ertuğrul. An Ottoman tomb initially in or near Qal'at Ja'bar has historically been associa
2 CONC ted with Suleyman Shah.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse	Hayme Hatun
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue	
2 CONT
2 CONT # Ertuğrul
2 CONT # Gündoğdu
2 CONT # Sungur-Tekin
2 CONT # Dündar
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Various sources linked Süleymanşâh to Osman Gazi and his father Ertuğrul.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT * He is mentioned in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atsiz '''Wikipedia page'''] of his father, Atsïz:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Issue'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Taj ad-Din Il-Arslan
2 CONT * Atliq
2 CONT * Hitan-Khan
2 CONT * '''Suleiman-Shah'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * “The historical adventure of the Tomb of Süleyman Shah.”  < [https://www.dailysabah.com/feature/2015/02/27/the-historical-adventure-of-the-tomb-of-suleyman-shah link] > Daily Sabah.  (FEB 27, 2015).  “… But what is the name of t
2 CONC his glorious person who is the ancestor of an empire that ruled over parts of three continents for six centuries? While some Ottoman historians claim that he is '''Süleyman Shah''', others claim it is '''Gündüz Alp'''. ''Both argu
2 CONC ments are most likely true as the first name is an Arabic name and the latter is a Turkic name''….”
