2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia: Alexandru Lăpuşneanu was Prince of Moldavia between September 1552 and 18 November 1561 and then between October 1564 and 5 May 1568. His wife and consort was Ruxandra, the daughter of Peter IV Rareş and Princess Jelena
2 CONC  Branković (the second daughter of Jovan Branković of Serbia).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the original founder of the Dormition Church, Lviv, also commonly known as the Wallachian Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is known as Alexandru IV Lapusneanu
