2 CONT '''Adil Giray (Girey) (1617 - 1672) Khan of Crimea in 1666-1671.''' Also known as Adil Choban-Gerai and Chul-Boldu. Adil Giray is the only khans of Crimea who belonged to the Choban-Gerai, a collateral branch of the Giray family.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to official genealogies, the Girays are Chingizids and descend from the Tugatimurids from Janak-oglan, the younger brother of Tui Khoja oglan, the father of Tokhtamysh. The eldest son of Janak oglan, Ichkile Hasan oglan,
2 CONC  is the father of Ulu Muhammad, the founder of the dynasty of Kazan Khans. However, this version of the origin of Hadji Giray encounters numerous inconsistencies. It is more likely that Hadji Giray was not a Chingizid, but belonge
2 CONC d to the famous Mongol-Turkic clan of Kerei (Kirei, Giray), and only later was the successful usurper attributed to the Golden clan.
