2 CONC me from a highly prominent non-titled provincial noble family with claims to a princely lineage, and their father owned 600 m.s., yet he was a mere NCO in the guards."[20: Igor Fedyukin. Nobility and Schooling in Russia, 1700s–176
2 CONC 0s: Choices in a Social Context. Journal of Social History, Volume 49, Number 3, Spring 2016, pp. 558-584. P. 576.].
