2 TITL Родословная схема дворянского рода Салтыковых XIV–XVIII в.
1 NOTE Tsar Alexis the first of Russia died January 29 1676.  He was succeeded by his son Fyodor III, who was in turn succeeded in 1682 by his brothers Ivan V and Peter I (the great) under the regency of Sophia.
1 NOTE Alexis I (1629-76), second Russian czar (1645-76) of the house of Romanov, 
2 CONT and father of Peter the Great. He succeeded his father Michael 
2 CONT (1596-1645). As a result of two campaigns by Alexis against the Poles 
2 CONT (1654-56 and 1660-67), Russia gained Smolensk, Kyyiv, and the lands east 
2 CONT of the Dnepr River. The war with Sweden (1656-58) was not as successful; 
2 CONT Alexis was forced to withdraw from the lands he had taken. The reign of 
2 CONT Czar Alexis was also marked by internal revolt, a schism in the Russian 
2 CONT Orthodox church, and the formulation of a legal code that extended the 
2 CONT serfdom of the Russian peasants.
