2 CONT
2 CONT Tsarevna Anna Mikhailovna of Russia was a Russian Tsarevna, daughter of Tsar Michael of Russia and Eudoxia Streshneva, and the sister of Tsar Aleksei I of Russia.
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT The inscription on her headstone reads: In the summer of 7201 October, on the 27th day on Wednesday against a quarter at five o'clock in the night, in memory of the holy martyr Nestor, the servant of God, the faithful and pious gr
2 CONC eat sovereign tsar and Grand Duke Mikhail Feodorovich of All Russia, autocrat and the faithful and noble Grand Empress Empress and Grand Duchess Evdokia Lukianovna, reposed Blessed Grand Duchess Princess and Grand Duchess Anna Mik
2 CONC hailovna was buried at this place on October 28th
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT Initially buried in the Ascension Monastery in Moscow but was moved to the Archangel Cathedral in 1929.
