1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/232752508/tatyana_mikhailovna-romanova
2 CONT
2 CONT Tatyana Mikhailovna of Russia was a Russian Tsarevna. She was heavily involved with the politics of the Romanov court during the reigns of her brother Alexis and the regency of her niece Sophia.
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT Inscription on the tombstone reads "In the summer of 7214 August against the 24th from Friday to Saturday at the night of the first hour in the last quarter, in memory of the holy martyr Eutychius, St. Princess Tatiana Mikhailovna
2 CONC  and was buried in this place on the same August 24 days and all the years of her life 71 years and 8 months." The inscription on the lid coincides with "The summer of the birth of Christ in 7214 August against the 24th of the nig
2 CONC ht of the first hour in the last quarter, in memory of the holy hieromartyr Eutychius, the servant of God, the blessed sovereign of the tsar and the great prince Mikhail Fedorovich of all Russia, the autocrat, the daughter of the 
2 CONC blessed sovereign princess and Grand Duchess Tatiana Mikhailovna and was buried at this place on August 24, and all the years of her life 72 years'"
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT Initially buried in the Ascension Monastery in Moscow but was moved to the Archangel Cathedral in 1929.
