1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LITHUANIA.htm#Sofiadied1453 Medlands]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sophia_of_Lithuania Sophia of Lithuania] (1371–1453) was a Grand Princess consort of Muscovy by marriage to Vasili I of Russia. She was regent of Muscovy during the minority of her son from 1425 to 1
2 CONC 434.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Life'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia (1371–1453) was the only daughter of Vytautas the Great of Lithuania and his first wife, Anna. On January 21, 1391, while her father was engaged in the Lithuanian Civil War, she married Vasili I of Russia. After his death i
2 CONC n 1425 she became regent of Moskovia for their ten-year old son Vasili II. Her father supported Vasili's claim to the throne, which was disputed by his uncle Yuri of Zvenigorod.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia was buried in the Ascension Convent; the sarcophagus was moved in 1929 to the Cathedral of the Archangel by Soviet authorities.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia and Vasili I of Russia had at least nine children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Anna of Moscow (1393 – August 1417), wife of John VIII Palaiologos  
2 CONT # Yury Vasilievich (30 March 1395 – 30 November 1400)  
2 CONT # Ivan Vasilievich (15 January 1396 – 20 July 1417), husband of a daughter of Ivan Vladimirovich of Pronsk  
2 CONT # Anastasia Vasilievna (d. 1470), wife of Vladymir Alexander, Prince of Kiev. Her husband was a son of Vladymir, Prince of Kiev. His paternal grandparents were Algirdas and Maria of Vitebsk.  
2 CONT # Daniil Vasilievich (6 December 1400 – May 1402).  
2 CONT # Vasilisa Vasilievna, wife of Alexander Ivanovich "Brukhaty", Prince of Suzdal, and Alexander Daniilovich "Vzmetenj", Prince of Suzdal  
2 CONT # Simeon Vasilievich (13 January – 7 April 1405)  
2 CONT # Maria Vasilievna, wife of Yuri Patrikievich. Her husband was a son of Patrikej, Prince of Starodub and his wife Helena. His paternal grandfather was Narimantas.  
2 CONT # Vasily II of Moscow (10 March 1415 – 27 March 1462) 
