1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Princess (Shahzadi ‘Alamiyan) Shahbanu Begum. married in Isfahan, 5th April 1713, as his first wife, Sayyid Mirza Muhammad Daud al-Husaini al-Marashi (b. at Isfahan, 25th January 1655; there, before 27th December 1
2 CONC 715), Mutawali of the Shrine of the Imam Reza at Mashhad, eldest son of Sayyid ‘Abdu’llah al-Husaini al-Marashi, by his wife Princess ‘Izz-i-Sharaf, daughter of H.M. Simon II, King of Kartli. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in Isfahan, 13th December 1738, having had issue, two sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sayyid ‘Abu’l Qasim Mirza al-Husaini al-Marashi. He had issue two sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sayyid Mirza Ahmad, who succeeded as H.M. Shah Ahmad I, Shahanshah of Persia – see below.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sayyid Mirza ‘Abdu’l Aimra. He was killed with his brother, August 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sayyid Sultan Muhammad Mirza Safawi, who succeeded as H.M. king (Shah) Suleiman II, Shahanshah of Persia
2 CONT
2 CONT Unnamed daughter, had issue, a son;
2 CONT
2 CONT Latif Khan. He d. after, 1724.
