1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Daud_Khan_Undiladze https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daud_Khan_Undiladze
2 CONT
2 CONT Daud-Khan or Dāvūd b. Allāhverdī (Persian: داوود خان, Georgian: დაუდ-ხანი) was a Safavid Iranian military commander and politician of Georgian origin who served as governor (beglarbeg) of Ganja and Karabakh from 1627 to 1633.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daud Khan was the son of Allahverdi Khan, a former Georgian gholam ("military slave") from the Undiladze clan who rose through the highest ranks in the Safavid administration under Shah Abbas I of Persia (r. 1588-1629). Daud-Khan,
2 CONC  unlike his father and older brother, Imam-Quli Khan, had closer ties with the country of his origin; he was married to Helene, the sister of the Georgian king Teimuraz I of Kakheti (Tahmuras Khan), and was on friendly terms with 
2 CONC the Georgian warlord Giorgi Saakadze (Murav Beg). Daud-Khan tried to mediate a conflict between Abbas I and the shah's recalcitrant Georgian subjects. After Shah Safi succeeded upon the death of Abbas in 1629, the new shah's mento
2 CONC r and yet another influential Georgian at the Safavid court, Khosrow Mirza, succeeded in sidelining the rival Undiladze clan, and persuaded Safi into removing Daud-Khan from the majles in 1630/31. In 1633, alarmed by the political
2 CONC  purges within the Iranian ruling élite, Daud fled to Georgia, where he apparently encouraged his brother-in-law Teimuraz I to renew his rebellion against the Safavid overlordship. Daud claimed that one of his brothers was actuall
2 CONC y the son of the late shah Abbas I and that he, having 30,000 troops under his command, had already conquered all of Fars, Bahrain, Lar, Hormuz, Khuzestan, Arabestan, and Hoveyzeh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Teimuraz and Daud started to attack the Persian garrisons in and near Georgia and launched several raids on Ganja of which Daud-Khan had been dispossessed after his defection to Georgia. Teimuraz refused to surrender Daud in excha
2 CONC nge of the shah's parole and allowed him a free passage to the Ottoman possessions. Since then, he disappears from the records. His brother and nephews were annihilated, and Daud's sons castrated on the shah's order, thus largely 
2 CONC ending the career of this illustrious Iranian Georgian family.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daud_Khan_Undiladze
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikizero.com/az/Davud_xan_Undiladze Davud khan Undiladze is a Safavid commander of Georgian origin. His father Allahverdi khan I was the jeweler of Shah Abbas Safavid. David Khan also joined the Shah's slave guard. The
2 CONC n he became the prince of the Karabakh principality.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a Georgian source, the insane Davud khan Shah was expelled from the banquet several times. The allies, who suddenly invaded Ganja, killed the soldiers of the Gajar fortress garrison here and "swore to capture all of A
2 CONC zerbaijan." The Armenian Catholicos, who joined the Allies, addressed Teymur with the following "idea": Loot Tabriz until it opposes you, change the khans in power in Azerbaijan, and then send me to Khotkar so that I can get troop
2 CONC s from it. Even if the Shah enters the battle, he will not be able to win, because it is impossible for the Georgians to retreat, they will know they have lost. If they retreat, the Red Army will overtake them on this long journey
2 CONC . Therefore, the Georgians will fight with all their might and you will win. You will be a great tyrant, and through you the Christian world will gain freedom and power. " Teymuraz, who did not lag behind the Armenian Catholicos i
2 CONC n his cunning, replied: "I will take you and Davud khan with me to Gori."
2 CONT
2 CONT Davud khan was killed by Shah Safi I Safavi in ​​1633 because he looted the province in 1633 and fled to the Ottoman region.
