2 CONC edaliah Ha-Zaken, and 2) Yosef Ha-Meshorer. Shlomo was a philosopher and royal military advisor. He was concerned about the extravagant life style of the community and tried to convince his fellow Jews to curtail their ostentatiou
2 CONC s display of wealth. He saw the love of luxury as eating away at the soul of the people and was fearful that it could arouse the wrath of the gentile population.
