2 CONT '''Gjin/Jhon Bua Shpata/Spata''' 
2 CONT Shapta / Spata Name; The word spata, in Albanian shpatë, pl. shpata, 'sword'.[1] According to Orel (1998), the word was borrowed from Latin spāta.[2] Hammond thus believes that he was called 
2 CONT '''John the Sword''' as Spatha/Spata being a type of Roman sword.
2 CONT ..recognized as a ruler in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epirus Epirus] and Aetolia by [https://www.geni.com/people/Simeon-Uro%C5%A1-despot-of-Epirus-Thessaly/6000000002188625349 Simeon Uroš] in 1359–1360.
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ioannina Ioannina] the capital of Preljubović, came under constant siege and was blocked by the Mazaraki and Malakasi clans under Losha.[5][6] A truce was signed when Pjetër’s son Gjin was betrothed 
2 CONC to Thomas's daughter Irina.[5][7] She died in the 1375 plague that affected the region and hostilities began again.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Spata
2 CONT John Spata (Albanian: Gjin Bua Shpata) (fl. 1358 – 29 October 1399) was an Albanian ruler in western Greece with the title of Despot. Together with Peter Losha, he led raids into Epirus, Acarnania and Aetolia in 1358. He was recog
2 CONC nized as Despot by titular Serbian Emperor Simeon Uroš in the early 1360s and ruled Aetolia (1360s–?), Angelokastron (?–1399), Naupactus (1378–99), and Arta (1370s–99).
2 CONT He was married to a woman who is unknown in historical record.[22] He had an only daughter, Irene who was married (before April 1381 ) to a Marchesano of Naples, Morean baron, baillie of Achaea[23] and Esau de' Buondelmonti in 139
2 CONC 6.[20] Esau was the Despot of Ioannina.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
