1 NOTE Ivan Alexander Shishman succeeded Ivan Shishman to power in Bulgaria in 1331.  Ivan Alexander ruled until 1371.  He was succeeded by Ivan Stratsimi, his son.  Ivan Alexander maintained friendly relations with Serbia.  His sister, 
2 CONC Yelena, was married to Dushan the powerful ruler of Serbia.  During Ivan Alexander's reign his country was attacked frequently by the Turkish forces.  During his reign he divided Bulgaria into two provinces ruled by his two sons, 
2 CONC Stratsimir, who ruled Vidin and Norwestern Bulgaria (1365-1371), and the younger son Ivan Shishman III who ruled central Bulgaria (1371-1393). Northeastern Bulgaria (Dobruja) became an independent state.
