1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Kantakouzenos_(died_1316)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Michael Kantakouzenos''' (Greek: Μιχαὴλ Καντακουζηνός, romanized: Mikhaḗl Kantakouzēnós; died 1316) was the first epitropos ("steward, overseer") of the Byzantine province of the Morea, a position he held from 1308 till his dea
2 CONC th in 1316.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1308, Byzantine emperor Andronikos II Palaiologos passed a decree, which stopped the appointment of new governors of the Morea every year and that this position be given to one person until his death. After the decree was passe
2 CONC d, the first epitropos the emperor appointed was Michael Kantakouzenos. His coming to the Morea was a blessing for the local population in the poor province because he stopped the practice of corrupt governors who tried to pull of
2 CONC f a "get rich quick" scheme in their 12-month term. He enabled economic stabilization within the province in his short eight-year term, giving his successor, Andronikos Asen, the possibility of starting a war of conquest.
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael Kantakouzenos married Theodora Palaiologina Angelina, possible daughter of General Chandrenos and wife Theodote Glabaina Tarchaneiotissa, and died in 1316. His son John became emperor in 1347. His wife died under house arr
2 CONC est in Constantinople on 6 January 1342 and was buried in the Convent of Kyra-Martha.
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2012611453.htm#Kantadied1294MTheodoraAP
2 CONT
2 CONT    [Four] siblings, parents not known: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         '''--- Kantakouzenos''' ([1264/65]-1294).  According to Sturdza[506], his possible name was Mikhael but the basis for this speculation is not known.  Emperor Andronikos II appointed him governor of Mistra, styled "capta
2 CONC in of the land and castles in the Peloponnesos".  Miller specifies that he was killed in 1316 after governing the province for eight years[507], which is inconsistent with the death date shown here as stated in Europäische Stammta
2 CONC feln[508].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' THEODORA Angelina Palaiologina, daughter of --- (-6 Jan 1342).  Ioannes Kantakouzenos names "Theodora Palaeologina…magni…domestici matre", stating that she was "cognata" of Emperor Andronikos II[509].  Another clue to her 
2 CONC parentage is provided by Ioannes Kantakouzenos who names "uno enim magistro avunculo nostro Angelo magno stratopedarcha", "nostro" apparently referring both to "magnus domesticus" who is the speaker in this section of the text and
2 CONC  is identified with the author, the future Emperor Ioannes VI Kantakouzenos, and to "Syrgiannes"[510].  She may have been the granddaughter of a sister of Emperor Mikhael VIII[511].  Ioannes Kantakouzenos records that "Archontes" 
2 CONC imprisoned "matrem magni domestici cum nepote Andronico", in a passage dated to [1341][512].  
2 CONT
2 CONT    --- Kantakouzene & his wife had one child:
2 CONT *a)         IOANNES Palaiologos Angelos Komnenos Kantakouzenos ([1294/95]-Mistra 15 Jun 1383).  His parentage is confirmed by his own History which names "Theodora Palaeologina…magni…domestici matre", stating that she was "cognata
2 CONC " of Emperor Andronikos II[513].  He was proclaimed Emperor IOANNES VI in 1341.  -        see below, Part B. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
