2 CONT # https://www.britannica.com/topic/Contarini-family '''Contarini family,''' distinguished Venetian family, one of the 12 that elected the first doge in 697 and later gave Venice eight doges and many other eminent citizens. There w
2 CONC ere at one time no fewer than 18 branches of the family; one of the most important was that of Contarini dallo Zaffo, or di Giaffa, who had been invested with the countship of Jaffa in Syria for their services to Caterina Cornaro,
2 CONC  queen of Cyprus; ...
