1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONFERRATO,%20SALUZZO,%20SAVONA.htm#Flaminiodied1571B
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Flaminio-Paleologo/6000000208081864831 FLAMINIO Paleologo], illegitimate son of GIAN GIORGIO SEBASTIANO Marchese di Monferrato & his mistress --- (-24 May 1571).  Signor di San Giorgio e Caluso 1532.  
2 CONC He served in the Spanish army.  Governor of Casale and Senator 1559.  He claimed the throne of Monferrato in 1568 and was imprisoned. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' LUCIA Fanzini, daughter of SIGISMONDO Fanzini, from Mantua [Governor of Casale 1539] & his wife ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Flaminio & his wife had eight children: 
2 CONT *1.         GIOVANNI (-1540, bur Monteu). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *2.         LAURA .  m (before 11 Jul 1589) ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *3.         MARGHERITA .  m (before 11 Jul 1589) [---, son of TEODORO Scazzoso]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *4.         TEODORO .  He was ambassador of Ercole Gonzaga in 1536.  Knight of the Order of Malta.  He was at Novi in 1568, but fled to Spain[381]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *5.         FLAMINIO .  He was ancestor of the family PALEOLOGHI-ORIUNDI[382]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *6.         ISABELLA (-before 11 Jul 1589). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *7.         ELEONORA (-before 11 Jul 1589). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *8.         FERDINANDO .  He served the Gonzaga family[383].  m ---.  The name of Ferdinando's wife is not known.  Ferdinando & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT **a)     '''    BERNARDINO''' (-before 1630).  m ---.  The name of Bernardino's wife is not known.  Bernardino & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT ***i)          BONIFAZIO ([1583/84]-2 Dec 1630).  m ---.  The name of Bonifazio's wife is not known.  Bonifazio & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT ****(a)       BONIFAZIO .  1679.  He was court surgeon at Casale[384].  m ---, daughter of GIAMBATTISTA Bobina & his wife ---.  Bonifazio & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *****(1)       GIAMBATTISTA Paleologo .  1687.  He was court surgeon at Casale[385].  Ancestor of SILVIO, who lived around 1900[386]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
