1 TITL Prince
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Biography''' Prince Boris Golitsyn was born in 1705 to Prince Vasily Borisovich Golitsyn (1681-1710) and Princess Anna Alexseevna, nee Rzhevskaya (1680-1705)  In 1718, Boris began service in the Imperial NAvy as
2 CONC  a midshipman and a few years later was promoted to warrant officer. According to the historian Prince MM Shcherbatov, BV Golitsyn "''had some occasion at the cour''t" , which may have contributed to his career. He became chief-se
2 CONC chmeister in1746 & in 1755: Vice Admiral &''General-Kriegscommander'' of the Russian Imperial fleet. At one time, Boris Golitsyn was also Chief Artillery Commander ''Feldtsikhmeister General'' (later this post became the exclusive
2 CONC  prerogative of members of the imperial family). On April 30, 1762, Prince Boris Vasilyevich Golitsyn retired for health reasons with the rank of full Admiral  In 1767, the Prince was elected a deputy from the Council of Nobles of
2 CONC  the Kaluga & Medynsky districts of the Moscow province to the Commission of Jurisprudence in drafting a new coda of laws for Russia. However, at the fourth meeting, on August 8,1767, in the Faceted Chamber of the Moscow Kremlin, 
2 CONC he "for poor health" handed over his deputy to the adjutant general, Prince IP Tyufyakin [3] .Prince Boris Vasilievich Golitsyn died the following year on July 12, 1768. .
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family''' In 1726 Boris Golitsyn married Sophia (Ekaterina) Ivanovna Streshneva (1701-1739). with whom he fathered Nine children (four daughters and five sons(.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Estates''' According to the record bookss of the second revision (1744-1747), Boris Vasilyevich Golitsyn was the founder and first owner of the estate: Kosmodemyanovskoye-Golitsyno, and its adjoining village of Vasilyevskaya Sl
2 CONC oboda (now the village of Nizhneye Golitsyno,, Rtishchevsky district ). The patrimonial allotment went to him as a dowry in 1726 from his wife Sophia* Streshneva (who pre-deceased him in 1739) who inherited this estate from her gr
2 CONC andfather, Senator Tikhon Nikitich Streshnev (1644-1719). and which by1745 had 128 male souls. Upon her death Prince Boris Golitsyno also inherited the Uzkoye estate near Moscow.
2 CONT >In''Streshnev'' family trees her name is''Sophia'' but in listings of the'' Golitsyns'' she's shown as ''Ekaterina''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His Awards & Honors''':
2 CONT Order of the Holy Grand Duke Alexander Nevsky (March 30, 1757) [1] [8] Order of St. Anne, 1st class [1]
