2 CONT Prince Alexander Alexandrovich Prozorovsky (Russian: Алекса́ндр Алекса́ндрович Прозоро́вский) (1732–1809) was the only Field Marshal from the Prozorovsky family. He gained distinction in the Seven Years' War and the conquest of Cr
2 CONC imea. Prozorovsky's career was furthered by his maternal Galitzine relatives, who helped him to get appointed to the office of Kursk's governor in 1780.
