1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Şehzade Ömer (20 October 1621 - January 1622) was an Ottoman prince (Turkish: şehzade), son of Sultan Osman II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Şehzade Ömer was born on 20 October 1621, to Sultan Osman II and Meylişah Hatun. On Osman's way back he had received the news that he had a son born. Now as a father, he had a successor and posed a threat against his brothers. He 
2 CONC called her to Edirne where the two met and Osman had the chance to see his son, Ömer. To celebrate the auspicious moment and possibly to impress her, he ordered a festivity to be held. In the celebrations, imitation of the battle 
2 CONC scenes was a part of the show. Yet the unimaginable happened and the baby suddenly died. Some history writers explain this event by the shock the infant had due to noises of the fired cannons.[1] Hammer gives a more striking reaso
2 CONC n for the baby's death: "To increase her joy festivities were held and some scenes of the Polish war were staged. The prince was present in these games and by the sudden shot from a rifle [by coincidence] he was wounded and died."
2 CONC [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT See also
2 CONT
2 CONT     Ottoman Empire
2 CONT     Ottoman dynasty
2 CONT     Ottoman family tree
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT Altınay, Ahmet Refik, Kadınlar Saltanatı, c.1, (Istanbul, Tarih Vakfı Yurt Yay., 2000), p.103 Hammer, p.309
