1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Öküz" Mehmed Pasha ("Mehmed Pasha the Ox"; died 23 December 1619), also known as Kara Mehmed Pasha ("the Black") or "Kul Kıran" Mehmed Pasha ("the Slavebreaker"),[1] was an Ottoman statesman, administrator and mil
2 CONC itary figure of the early 17th century who held the office of Grand Vizier twice, the first time from 17 October 1614 to 17 November 1616 (during the reign of Ahmed I) and the second time from 18 January 1619 to 23 December 1619 (
2 CONC during the reign of Osman II the Young).[2] He was also governor of Egypt from 1607 to 1611.[1][3][4][5][6] Okuz Mehmed's nickname "Kul Kiran" (slavebreaker) came from his success in crushing the mutiny in Egypt during the early 1
2 CONC 600s (soldiers were often known as kul or slave). 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%96k%C3%BCz_Mehmed_Pasha En], [https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%96k%C3%BCz_Mehmed_Pa%C5%9Fa Tr]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Note''': Wikipedia link redirects for "Kara Mehmed Pasha" redirects here. For the later Ottoman governor of Egypt (and other provinces), see [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kara_Mehmed_Pasha_(died_1722)_ Kara Mehmed Pasha (died 
2 CONC 1722)].
2 CONT In this Ottoman Turkish style name, the given name is Mehmed, the title is Pasha, and there is no family name.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT He was of Turkish origin and was born in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karag%C3%BCmr%C3%BCk Karagümrük] district of Istanbul. It is reported that his father was an ox blacksmith.[7][8][9] He was nicknamed "Black" and also given t
2 CONC he nickname "Ox" by is enemies, based on the profession of his father.[10] Before holding governmental positions, Mehmed Pasha had been a silahdar, a high-ranking position in the sultan's guard.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married princess [https://www.geni.com/people/Gevherhan-Sultan/6000000046818659076 Gevherhan Sultan], the daughter of sultan [https://www.geni.com/people/Ahmed-I/385240598850012788 Ahmed I] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Mahp
2 CONC eyker-K%C3%B6sem-Sultan/385243216040011958 Kösem Sultan]. They had a son died in infancy.[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%96k%C3%BCz_Mehmed_Pasha#References References]===
