1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Topal Recep Pasha''' (Bosnian: Topal Redžep-paša, "Recep Pasha "Lame"; died 18 May 1632) was an Ottoman statesman from the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanjak_of_Bosnia Sanjak of Bosnia],[1] as well as Damat (
2 CONC "bridegroom") to the House of Osman. He served as the Grand Vizier of the Ottoman Empire from 10 February 1632 to 18 May 1632.[2] He was instrumental in lynching the former grand vizier, [https://www.geni.com/people/Haf%C4%B1z-Ahm
2 CONC ed-Pasha/6000000046842851467 Hafiz Ahmed Pasha]. When his brother-in-law Sultan [https://www.geni.com/people/Murad-IV/385243631930012754 Murad IV] realized this, he had Recep Pasha executed on 18 May 1632 in Constantinople.[3] He 
2 CONC was of Bosnian origin.[4] 
