1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Turhan Hatice Sultan''' (Ottoman Turkish: تورخان سلطان, "merciful" or "noble"; c. 1627 – 4 August 1683) was the first Haseki Sultan of the Ottoman Sultan Ibrahim (reign 1640–48) and Valide sultan as the mother o
2 CONC f Mehmed IV (reign 1648–87). Turhan was prominent for the regency of her young son and her building patronage. She and Kösem Sultan are the only two women in Ottoman history to be regarded as official regents and had supreme contr
2 CONC ol over the Ottoman Empire. As a result, Turhan became one of the prominent figures during the era known as Sultanate of Women. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turhan_Sultan En]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.myheritage.com.hr/names/hatice_osmano%C4%9Flu MH]
